+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; browsers display a revisioned view of the board. Committed changes reach browsers over self-hosted WebSockets, which gives fast updates without a realtime vendor. The project therefore owns connection capacity for up to 800 simultaneous browsers and the reconnect behavior of long-lived connections.
 
-Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery must be designed together after this choice. Polling would favor cursor queries; self-hosted sockets would need connection management and replay; hosted delivery would need publication reconciliation and provider credentials. Neither operating cost nor minimum operational burden has been declared the overriding criterion.
